As the sun beat down on the dusty roads of Stranglethorn Vale, Glimble Sparkspanner, a diminutive Gnome Warlock, led his Succubus, Xylara, through the dense jungle. They had been questing for hours, taking down mobs and collecting the necessary materials for Glimble's latest experiment. Xylara's Lash of Pain proved to be a valuable asset, taking down the occasional mob with a swift and silent strike. As they navigated the winding paths, Glimble couldn't help but feel a sense of pride in his Succubus's abilities. She was a loyal companion, and her stealth capabilities allowed them to sneak past many a mob undetected.

But as the day wore on, Glimble began to notice that many of the other Warlocks in the area were accompanied by Voidwalkers. He wondered why they would choose such a...tactically inferior pet.

The reason most Warlocks are seen with Voidwalkers is because of the social aspect of the game. Voidwalkers have a unique ability to taunt and generate threat, which can be useful in PvP situations, such as dueling or battlegrounds. Additionally, Voidwalkers have a more aggressive and intimidating appearance, which can be seen as a status symbol among players. Succubus, on the other hand, is often seen as a more " PvE" pet, better suited for soloing and questing. [end of text]


